From c2e539e4ad73d0ac85390c59c88eb526a501c632 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Isaku Yamahata <isaku.yamahata@intel.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Dec 2021 18:51:26 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 083/164] KVM: TDX: Handle vCPU migration over logical
 processor

Flush the address translation caches and cached TD VMCS associated with a
TD vCPU when the vCPU is de-associating with its current logical processor.

For vCPU migration, in the case of VMX, VMCS is flushed on the source pCPU
via VMCLEAR, and loaded on the target pCPU via VMPTRLD.  In the case of TDX,
the SEAMCALL TDH.VP.FLUSH is used to break the association between a vCPU
and a logical processor, flushes the vCPU's TD VMCS to TDVPS memory and
flushes the vCPU's TLB ASID.  Do it on the source pCPU.  After the SEAMCALL
TDH.VP.FLUSH is done, the vCPU is not associated with any logical processor.
Any following vCPU specific SEAMCALL (e.g., TDH.VP.ENTER) on the destination
pCPU will create a new association between the vCPU and the new logical
processor.

When shutting down the machine, (VMX or TDX) vCPUs need to be shutdown on
each pCPU.  De-associate the vCPUs for TDX with the TDX SEAMCALL.

Signed-off-by: Isaku Yamahata <isaku.yamahata@intel.com>
