From 95a0f656ceb876dc69520a83551f17d99a355296 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Isaku Yamahata <isaku.yamahata@intel.com>
Date: Fri, 31 May 2024 17:58:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 090/164] KVM: TDX: Wait lapic expire when POSTED_INTR_ON set

Call kvm_wait_lapic_expire() when POSTED_INTR_ON is set before TD entry.

Since APIC state is protected for TDX guest, KVM always assumes a timer
IRQ was injected when deciding whether or not to busy wait in
kvm_wait_lapic_expire().  Call kvm_wait_lapic_expire() only when
POSTED_INTR_ON is set to reduce unnecessary wait.

Signed-off-by: Isaku Yamahata <isaku.yamahata@intel.com>
Signed-off-by: Binbin Wu <binbin.wu@linux.intel.com>
---
v20:
- Split out from patch "KVM: TDX: Implement interrupt injection". (Chao)
